=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
No fault exists in the network. The user's claim that Laptop0 (172.16.20.10)
is blocked from reaching the 172.16.10.x subnet is factually incorrect. Direct
probes show full bidirectional reachability: laptop0 reaches pc4 (172.16.10.4)
and pc5 (172.16.10.5) with 0% packet loss and TTL=63, confirming exactly one
router hop as expected. The reverse direction (pc4 → laptop0) is also clean at
0% loss.

Router0 is the inter-VLAN gateway for both subnets, with two 802.1Q
sub-interfaces in place and UP: eth0.10 (172.16.10.1/24) serving VLAN 10 and
eth0.20 (172.16.20.1/24) serving VLAN 20. The FRR running configuration
contains no access-lists, no route-maps, and no prefix-filters of any kind —
only a RIP process advertising the relevant networks. The Linux kernel iptables
FORWARD chain on router0 is policy ACCEPT with zero deny rules. No nftables
filter applies to inter-VLAN traffic either.

The ticket describes an ACL block "on the router between my group and theirs,"
but no such filter exists anywhere in the datapath. The user's perception is
incorrect — the network is healthy, the subnets can communicate freely, and no
corrective action is warranted. The helpdesk should close this ticket and advise
the user to verify their workstation's local configuration (firewall, routing,
or ARP cache) as the most likely source of any application-layer issue they
observed.
=== END ===
